  "conclusions": [
    "One shared low-score rejection threshold cannot remove any of the 48 unmatched baseline events or 60 hybrid kick-free events while preserving every existing full-history tight hit in this development set. This is an optimistic label-informed bound, not a proposed threshold.",
    "Late Night fails the hoped-for ghost separation: hit median 0.215 versus hybrid kick-free median 0.204, with overlapping ranges. Its within-track ranking AUC is 0.522, approximately uninformative in this sample.",
    "Midnight shows better within-track separation (AUC 0.947 against hybrid ghosts), but that does not transfer to Late Night or establish generalisation. No track-specific settings were chosen.",
    "Bad Guy unwanted attacks produce stronger novelty than kicks: median 0.515 versus 0.286. Prediction error measures changes, not instrument identity.",
    "There is evidence near missed events: the Inhale 12.620 s label has a nominal peak at +20 ms; the two late Feel hits have peaks at about +25-27 ms. These are oracle-selected peaks, not recovered triggers.",
    "Late Night missed-event maxima remain inside kick-free background ranges, and their strongest nominal peaks occur around +39-49 ms. More generic onset sensitivity does not solve those rolls safely.",
    "At 50 ms, missed-label versus kick-free-window ranking is 0.866 pooled, but relies on known onset windows, overlaps substantially and is sensitive to label alignment. It must not be presented as 86.6% kick accuracy.",
    "The measurement passes causal/numerical checks and looks useful on synthetic kicks, yet fails as a universal kick confirmation cue in these real mixtures. Do not add another threshold to the live detector on this evidence."
  ],
